WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:04.190
Speaker 1: Here's an interesting follow up
on a story from earlier this year.

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:08.610
Back in January, we covered this guy named
Christopher Dickey, who was promoting the

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:13.030
drinking of urine in order to treat or prevent
COVID.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:18.500
And we talked about it at the time, and I
explained to you then that a lot of this covered

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.089
quack stuff.

00:00:20.089 --> 00:00:24.189
It's a recycling of old ideas that have been
going around for a long time.

00:00:24.189 --> 00:00:29.350
Urine has been promoted in the past for treating
cancer, even though the Cancer Society says

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:33.720
there's no evidence at all for therapeutic
use of urine.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:39.390
They've talked about using urine to irrigate
the sinuses, almost like a pee neti pot for

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:44.860
brushing teeth, applying it directly to the
skin as a skin treatment of some kind.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:52.910
And the origins or the oranges of this urine
therapy thing is the idea that certain tumor

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:56.750
proteins are present in the urine of cancer
patients.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:04.800
And the idea is if you introduce urine into
the digestive tract by drinking it, the erroneous

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:11.360
belief is your body will make antibodies against
the tumor proteins and it'll destroy the cancer.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.320
That's like one example now there's no evidence
of that whatsoever.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:19.300
It's true that urine can contain tumor antigens.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:24.440
There's no evidence that drinking it, massaging
with it, bathing with it, cooking with it

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:28.770
or any other urine application is going to
stimulate antibody production in any way,

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:32.020
fight cancer or treat any symptom or disease.

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:37.170
So that was the idea before from Christopher
Qi was the drinking of urine.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:41.170
He's now moved on to promoting injecting urine.

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:47.650
Here is a clip of him at least claiming that
he's injecting himself with aged urine.

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:50.390
You know how sometimes people will age stakes.

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:51.640
This is aged urine.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.440
Speaker 4: I'm doing it for muscular.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:59.619
I have your eye dying, but I'm just going
to sterilize it with my own urine, right?

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.700
And and what not to talk about the stem cells,
right?

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.760
Speaker 1: All right.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:07.119
So and as this is going on, you see him take
out a syringe.

00:02:07.119 --> 00:02:13.079
Speaker 4: So pretty much every every type
of stem cell is available in your urine.

00:02:13.079 --> 00:02:20.470
So stem cells are the base pure DNA cells
that will start replicating.

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:24.780
Yeah, additional cells for regeneration and
repair.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:28.709
I mean, everybody's hearing about regeneration
repair.

00:02:28.709 --> 00:02:33.939
People are flying to Thailand to get stem
cell injections done over there.

00:02:33.939 --> 00:02:34.939
Yeah.

00:02:34.939 --> 00:02:44.239
Speaker 1: So the idea there is that Christopher
Qi has injected himself with urine, and some

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:47.909
people wrote to me saying, David, he clearly
isn't really injecting himself.

00:02:47.909 --> 00:02:51.290
I don't think it matters because if people
believe it, it's dangerous.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:56.140
And this is all from the same school of thought
that sometimes includes homeopathy.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:03:00.360
Sometimes it includes, you know, some of these
other.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.269
I'm not going to rap too much, either.

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:03.340
This is what it is.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:08.810
OK, now this is extraordinarily dangerous
if you, you know, Christopher Qi said he's

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:11.150
injecting the urine intramuscularly.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:17.219
If you inject urine into a vein, it can get
very bad, very quickly.

00:03:17.219 --> 00:03:24.519
There's actually a study called lethal sepsis
and multiorgan failure after accidental injection

00:03:24.519 --> 00:03:31.319
of urine in a drug addict, and the story is
about a 33 year old drug addict that injected

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:36.920
urine because he kept it in the fridge in
case he needed it for a drug screening.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:40.849
And then he thought it was methadone and injected
it, and it went into a vein and was confused

00:03:40.849 --> 00:03:44.439
and shivering and had all sorts of different
symptoms.

00:03:44.439 --> 00:03:45.889
Sepsis, it was crazy.

00:03:45.889 --> 00:03:50.689
OK, so this is all extraordinarily dangerous,
and they just don't seem to be stopping now.

00:03:50.689 --> 00:03:53.809
I genuinely wonder, like, are they really
making money with this?

00:03:53.809 --> 00:03:54.809
I don't know.

00:03:54.809 --> 00:03:59.189
The guy who's interviewing Christopher Key
here is Dr. Edward Group, and he runs some

00:03:59.189 --> 00:04:02.169
kind of natural healing thing.

00:04:02.169 --> 00:04:05.709
And does he make money promoting urine therapy?

00:04:05.709 --> 00:04:06.709
I just don't know.

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:11.189
I don't I don't know exactly like what the
what the money piece is now.

00:04:11.189 --> 00:04:17.519
As I've said before, there is one possible
legitimate life-saving use of urine, and it

00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:23.460
is as follows If you are completely dehydrated,
you're without water, you're on the verge

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:24.720
of dying.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:31.180
There is a short period during which drinking
your own urine could extend your life just

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:34.510
enough to be rescued or to get to water right.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:41.760
Urine is 95 percent water, and it's believed
that drinking your own urine might allow you

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:45.020
to survive an extra day or two.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:47.449
It is strictly speaking, safe.

00:04:47.449 --> 00:04:49.970
It replenishes some lost water.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:55.070
But the problem is the other five percent
of urine that's not water is not something

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:56.790
you want a lot of in your body, right?

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:59.539
You're taking the stuff that your kidneys
have filtered.

00:04:59.539 --> 00:05:04.199
Out, and you're putting it back in and putting
it back into your kidneys, and this can cause

00:05:04.199 --> 00:05:07.110
really bad symptoms and long, long term problems.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:12.650
But if there's anything that in the urine
therapy world, we would say is sort of legit.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:19.470
It would be you might extend a deadly situation
with no water by a day or two.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:21.039
And that's basically it.

00:05:21.039 --> 00:05:21.280
Absolutely horrifying stuff.

